# Unreal packages are binary even before Git LFS is available.
*.uasset filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.umap filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Run `sh Tools/enable_git_lfs.sh` after Git LFS is installed. It appends the
# LFS filters for future packages. It does not migrate history.
# Canon reference images - binary, versioned via LFS like the packages.
Docs/canon/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Docs/canon/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Docs/canon/*.webp filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
# Donor texture SOURCES under Tools/textures - CC0 maps kept for custody, and
# the intermediates generated from them. These are large binaries and belong
# in LFS for the same reason the packages do.
#
# ADDED 2026-08-31 AFTER FINDING THE HOLE: the brick sources committed on
# 2026-08-28 matched NO pattern here and went into git proper as raw blobs -
# `git cat-file` shows a PNG header, not an LFS pointer. That is the same
# wound .git already carries from the two pre-LFS commits, made a second time
# because the canon images got a rule and this directory never did. The
# existing brick blobs stay where they are: removing them is a history
# rewrite, which is a hard stop.
Tools/textures/source/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Tools/textures/source/**/*.jpg filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
Tools/textures/source/**/*.exr filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
